export anchor FarmersMarketStyle:
    number: 84
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Farmers market
    idea: A Saturday market stall where projects sit in wooden crates filled with produce to their progress, the week's numbers hang as price tags on twine, and every sign looks hand painted.
    base: light
    palette:
        canvas: #f5eedf, the page
        pine: #ecd3a2, the header board, crates and section signs
        pineShade: #c9a46a, slat lines and last week bars, never text
        kraft: #e2c99a, nav slats and slip edges
        tagCard: #fffaf0, price tags, activity slips, crate feet and fields
        ink: #2a1f14, text and outlines
        soil: #5a4632, crate frames and small notes
        twine: #9b7b4f, strings and tag cords, never text
        leaf: #2f5d2a, the brand, the current nav slat, On track, this week bars and focus
        carrot: #9a4a08, At risk and Marketing produce
        tomato: #a3261b, the New project button, overdue and Behind
        plum: #5b2a5e, Research produce
    type:
        Three stacks. Signs use Cooper Black, Bookman Old Style, Rockwell
        Extra Bold, Georgia, serif at 400 for the 46px greeting, 52px price
        tag numbers, 34px brand, 24px section signs, 26px crate percentages
        and 20px crate names in caps. Handwriting uses Segoe Print, Bradley
        Hand, Chalkboard SE, Comic Sans MS, cursive at 15 to 20px for dates,
        tag captions, due dates and times. Body uses Trebuchet MS, Gill
        Sans, Segoe UI, sans-serif at 16px with 1.5 line height, and status
        words at 14px bold.
    layout:
        A striped green and cream awning with a scalloped edge runs across
        the top. Under it a pine header board with plank lines holds a
        tomato brand mark, the brand, a tag shaped search field, the New
        project button, a round bell and the user. A dark rail carries the
        nav as small kraft slats hung on two twine strings each. The
        greeting is a big painted line with the date in handwriting, and a
        red tag tilted 2 degrees on the right says 4 tasks are overdue. The
        four numbers are price tags with a pointed left end and a punched
        hole, hung from a sagging twine line and alternately tilted. Below,
        a wide column titled On the stall holds six crates in a three
        column grid. Each crate has a painted end board with the name and
        team, a slatted strip filled from the left with produce dots in the
        team colour to the percentage, and a cream foot with percentage,
        due date, task count and status. The side column has a stall board
        of slightly tilted paper slips for activity and a framed bar chart
        whose bars are drawn as stacked crate slats. Below 960px the side
        column moves under the crates and tags go two by two.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between crates and tags, 40px between the two columns, 56px below the stall.
    density: Medium and chunky. Six big crates, four big tags and short slips.
    corners: 4 to 6px on boards and crates. Tags have a pointed end. Status chips are pills.
    borders: 2 to 3px soil or ink outlines on everything, slat lines inside wood, and a dashed ink edge where the produce stops.
    shadows: A flat 3px ink drop under buttons and tags, as if propped up. No blur.
    icons:
        Chunky filled shapes with ink outlines and a tomato brand mark.
        Status pills pair the word with a filled circle for On track, a
        filled triangle for At risk and a filled square for Behind.
        Overdue adds an exclamation octagon.
    focus: A 3px leaf outline offset 3px, then a canvas gap and a 2px ink ring out to 9px. A focused field turns its border leaf green.
    tone: A friendly stallholder, such as On the stall, Picked each day, ready to pick and pick these first.
